IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ada-dates`
IMPORT `ada-core`

-- Anti-Discrimination Act 1977 (NSW) -- THE SEAT OF THE PERSON WITH THE COMPLAINT: the job applicant, employee,
-- contractor or other worker who was discriminated against, sexually harassed, victimised or retired on the ground of
-- age, and who complains to the President of the Anti-Discrimination Board and may go on to the Civil and
-- Administrative Tribunal. Every question is asked as that person would ask it, from facts that person can state; the
-- judgments the Act leaves to the President, the Tribunal or a court are asked as conditions. The rules are in
-- ada-core.l4; this module restates none of them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website at 10 March 2025, via the Open Australian
-- Legal Corpus (version as at 1 July 2024). State of New South Wales, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE
-- ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Discrimination at work`

@export Was what my employer (or would-be employer) did to me unlawful discrimination under the NSW Anti-Discrimination Act, on the ground of race, sex, transgender grounds, marital or domestic status, disability, responsibilities as a carer, homosexuality or age?
GIVEN
    `the ground`                IS A `Ground`                @desc Which characteristic was it about? Race includes colour, nationality, descent and ethnic, ethno-religious or national origin; sex includes pregnancy and breastfeeding.
    `whose characteristic`      IS A `Whose characteristic`  @desc Was it about your own characteristic, or that of a relative (by blood, marriage, affinity, adoption or de facto partnership) or an associate (someone you associate with socially or in business, or who depends on you or lives in your household)?
    `the kind of disability`    IS A `Kind of disability`    @desc Only if the ground is disability: what kind of condition is it (one you, or your relative or associate, have, are thought to have, had in the past or will have)?
    `the person cared for`      IS A `Person cared for`      @desc Only if the ground is responsibilities as a carer: whom are your responsibilities to care for or support (ones you have, are thought to have, had or will have)?
    `the transgender description` IS A `Transgender description` @desc Only if the ground is transgender grounds: which describes you (or your relative or associate), whether or not the record of your sex has been altered?
    `the homosexuality description` IS A `Homosexuality description` @desc Only if the ground is homosexuality: are you (or your relative or associate) homosexual, or thought to be?
    `I was treated less favourably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you treated less favourably than the employer treats, or would treat, someone without that characteristic in circumstances that are the same or not materially different?
    `it was because of the characteristic` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the treatment on the ground of the characteristic, or of a trait generally belonging to or generally imputed to people who have it? It need only be one of the reasons (s 4A).
    `I was segregated`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if the ground is race: were you segregated from people of a different race on the ground of race?
    `I was required to meet a condition I cannot meet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employer require you to comply with a requirement or condition that you do not or cannot comply with?
    `far more people without the characteristic can meet it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do, or can, a substantially higher proportion of people without the characteristic comply with that requirement?
    `the condition is unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement not reasonable in the circumstances of the case? (A judgment for the Tribunal.)
    `my sex record has been altered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if the ground is transgender grounds: are you a recognised transgender person (the record of your sex altered under the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1995 or a corresponding law)?
    `I was treated as my former sex` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if you are a recognised transgender person: were you treated as being of your former sex?
    `far more people of my former sex can meet it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if you are a recognised transgender person: do, or can, a substantially higher proportion of people of your former sex comply with the requirement?
    `what the employer did`     IS A `What the employer did` @desc What did the employer do? Employment includes work under a contract for services.
    `it was for a private household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the employment for the purposes of the employer's private household?
    `the number of employees`   IS A NUMBER  @desc How many people does the employer employ, not counting anyone employed in its private household, and counting the employees of any related company?
    `it is a private school or college` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employer a private educational authority (a non-government school, college, university or other place of education or training)?
    `it was required by another law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what the employer did necessary to comply with another Act, a regulation or other instrument under one, or an order of the Tribunal or a court (not a minimum wage award)?
    `it was a religious body's act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it the ordination or appointment of a priest, minister or member of a religious order, training for that, or an appointment or act of a body established to propagate religion that conforms to its doctrines or is needed to avoid injury to its adherents' religious susceptibilities?
    `the job needs a particular race` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for race: does the job need a person of a particular race for authenticity (drama, modelling, a place serving food or drink), or provide welfare services to people of a race that are best given by a person of that race?
    `I am being trained for work outside NSW` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for race: are you not ordinarily resident in NSW, with the job meant to train you in skills you will use wholly outside NSW?
    `the job is on a ship or aircraft engaged outside NSW` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for race: is the job on a ship or aircraft, and were you engaged for it outside NSW?
    `it was a special needs program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for race or age: was it done to give people of a particular race or age group access to facilities, services or opportunities to meet their special needs?
    `sex or age is a genuine occupational qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for sex or age: is being of a particular sex (or age) a genuine occupational qualification for the job under the Act's tests (s 31, s 49ZYJ)? A judgment.
    `I am a man and it was a pregnancy-related right for a woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for sex: are you a man, and was it only that a woman was granted rights or privileges connected with pregnancy, childbirth or breastfeeding?
    `it was about super fund terms that meet the Act's test` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for sex, transgender grounds, marital or domestic status, disability or age: was it about the terms of a superannuation fund that meet the Act's superannuation exception for that ground (for example, based on reasonable actuarial data)?
    `the job is one of two for a married couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for marital or domestic status: is the job one of two to be held by a married couple?
    `it was an infectious disease and needed for public health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for disability: is the disability an infectious disease, and was the treatment reasonably necessary to protect public health?
    `I was addicted to a prohibited drug at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for disability: does the disability relate to addiction to a prohibited drug (not methadone or buprenorphine), and were you actually addicted at the time? (Hepatitis C, HIV or other conditions do not count.)
    `I could not do the job's inherent requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for disability or carer's responsibilities, and only for being refused the job or dismissed: because of it, would you be unable to carry out the inherent requirements of the job (taking account of your training, qualifications, experience and performance)? A judgment.
    `I would need adjustments that are an unjustifiable hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for disability or carer's responsibilities, and only for being refused the job or dismissed: would you need services, facilities or arrangements others do not need, whose provision would impose unjustifiable hardship on the employer? A judgment.
    `I was under 21`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for age: were you under 21?
    `it was a voluntary retirement scheme offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for age: was it an offer, made by reference to your length of service, to join a voluntary retirement, retirement incentive or voluntary severance scheme?
GIVETH A `Work answer`
`Was what my employer did unlawful discrimination` `the ground` `whose characteristic` `the kind of disability` `the person cared for` `the transgender description` `the homosexuality description` `I was treated less favourably` `it was because of the characteristic` `I was segregated` `I was required to meet a condition I cannot meet` `far more people without the characteristic can meet it` `the condition is unreasonable` `my sex record has been altered` `I was treated as my former sex` `far more people of my former sex can meet it` `what the employer did` `it was for a private household` `the number of employees` `it is a private school or college` `it was required by another law` `it was a religious body's act` `the job needs a particular race` `I am being trained for work outside NSW` `the job is on a ship or aircraft engaged outside NSW` `it was a special needs program` `sex or age is a genuine occupational qualification` `I am a man and it was a pregnancy-related right for a woman` `it was about super fund terms that meet the Act's test` `the job is one of two for a married couple` `it was an infectious disease and needed for public health` `I was addicted to a prohibited drug at the time` `I could not do the job's inherent requirements` `I would need adjustments that are an unjustifiable hardship` `I was under 21` `it was a voluntary retirement scheme offer` MEANS
    `the answer on discrimination in work` `the ground` `my characteristic` `my treatment` `what the employer did` `my employer` `my exceptions`
    WHERE
        `my characteristic` MEANS `Characteristic facts` WITH
            `whose characteristic`          IS `whose characteristic`
            `the kind of disability`        IS `the kind of disability`
            `the person cared for`          IS `the person cared for`
            `the transgender description`   IS `the transgender description`
            `the homosexuality description` IS `the homosexuality description`
        `my treatment` MEANS `Treatment facts` WITH
            `treated less favourably than a comparable person without the characteristic` IS `I was treated less favourably`
            `the treatment was on the ground of the characteristic` IS `it was because of the characteristic`
            `segregated on the ground of race` IS `I was segregated`
            `required to comply with a requirement or condition I do not or cannot comply with` IS `I was required to meet a condition I cannot meet`
            `a substantially higher proportion of people without the characteristic comply or can comply` IS `far more people without the characteristic can meet it`
            `the requirement is not reasonable in the circumstances` IS `the condition is unreasonable`
            `I am a recognised transgender person` IS `my sex record has been altered`
            `treated as being of my former sex` IS `I was treated as my former sex`
            `a substantially higher proportion of people of my former sex comply or can comply` IS `far more people of my former sex can meet it`
        `my employer` MEANS `Employer facts` WITH
            `the employment is for the purposes of the employer's private household` IS `it was for a private household`
            `the number of people the employer employs` IS `the number of employees`
            `the employer is a private educational authority` IS `it is a private school or college`
        `my exceptions` MEANS `Exception facts` WITH
            `it was necessary to comply with another Act, an instrument under one, or an order of the Tribunal or a court` IS `it was required by another law`
            `a religious bodies exception applies` IS `it was a religious body's act`
            `a person of a particular race is required for authenticity, or for welfare services best given by a person of that race` IS `the job needs a particular race`
            `I am not ordinarily resident in NSW and the job trains me in skills to be used wholly outside NSW` IS `I am being trained for work outside NSW`
            `the job is on a ship or aircraft and I was engaged for it outside NSW` IS `the job is on a ship or aircraft engaged outside NSW`
            `it was a special needs program for people of a particular race or age group` IS `it was a special needs program`
            `being of a particular sex or age is a genuine occupational qualification for the job` IS `sex or age is a genuine occupational qualification`
            `I am a man and it was a grant to a woman of rights connected with pregnancy, childbirth or breastfeeding` IS `I am a man and it was a pregnancy-related right for a woman`
            `it concerned superannuation fund terms that meet the Act's superannuation exception` IS `it was about super fund terms that meet the Act's test`
            `the job is one of two to be held by a married couple` IS `the job is one of two for a married couple`
            `the disability is an infectious disease and it was reasonably necessary to protect public health` IS `it was an infectious disease and needed for public health`
            `the disability relates to my addiction to a prohibited drug and I was actually addicted at the time` IS `I was addicted to a prohibited drug at the time`
            `I would be unable to carry out the inherent requirements of the job` IS `I could not do the job's inherent requirements`
            `I would need services, facilities or arrangements that would impose unjustifiable hardship on the employer` IS `I would need adjustments that are an unjustifiable hardship`
            `I was under 21` IS `I was under 21`
            `it was an offer, by length of service, to join a voluntary retirement or severance scheme` IS `it was a voluntary retirement scheme offer`

§ `Sexual harassment at work`
-- Situation: only if you were sexually harassed in connection with work.

@export Was I unlawfully sexually harassed at work under the NSW Anti-Discrimination Act?
GIVEN
    `what they did`             IS A `Sexual conduct`  @desc What did the person do to you? Unwelcome means you did not want or invite it.
    `a reasonable person would have expected me to be offended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances, have anticipated that you would be offended, humiliated or intimidated? A judgment.
    `who did it`                IS A `Who harassed me` @desc Who did it, and in what working relationship? A workplace participant is an employer, employee, commission agent, contract worker, partner, self-employed person, volunteer or unpaid trainee.
GIVETH A `Harassment answer`
`Was I unlawfully sexually harassed at work` `what they did` `a reasonable person would have expected me to be offended` `who did it` MEANS
    `the answer on sexual harassment at work` `what they did` `a reasonable person would have expected me to be offended` `who did it`

§ `Forced retirement because of age`
-- Situation: only if you have been retired, or pressed to retire.

@export Can my employer make me retire because of my age under the NSW Anti-Discrimination Act?
GIVEN
    `I am an employee in NSW`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an employee in New South Wales (including a commission agent or a contract worker)?
    `my office`                 IS A `My office` @desc Do you hold one of the offices to which the compulsory retirement rules do not apply?
    `what they did`             IS A `Retirement conduct` @desc What did the person do?
    `it was because of my age`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it on the ground of your age?
GIVETH A `Retirement answer`
`Can I be made to retire because of my age` `I am an employee in NSW` `my office` `what they did` `it was because of my age` MEANS
    `the answer on compulsory retirement` `I am an employee in NSW` `my office` `what they did` `it was because of my age`

§ `Victimisation`
-- Situation: only if you have complained, given evidence or otherwise used the Act, and something was done to you.

@export Was I unlawfully victimised for complaining, giving evidence or otherwise using the NSW Anti-Discrimination Act?
GIVEN
    `I suffered a detriment`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you subjected to a detriment (any disadvantage, such as being demoted, dismissed, excluded or threatened)?
    `what I did`                IS A `What I did under the Act` @desc What had you done, or intended to do, under the Act?
    `it was because of that`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the detriment on the ground of what you did, intended or were suspected of?
    `my allegation was false`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if it was an allegation: was the allegation false?
    `I made it in good faith`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if it was an allegation: did you make it in good faith?
GIVETH A `Victimisation answer`
`Was I unlawfully victimised` `I suffered a detriment` `what I did` `it was because of that` `my allegation was false` `I made it in good faith` MEANS
    `the answer on victimisation` `I suffered a detriment` `what I did` `it was because of that` `my allegation was false` `I made it in good faith`

§ `My employer's liability for what its staff did`

@export Is my employer (or principal) also liable for the discrimination or harassment its employee or agent did to me under the NSW Anti-Discrimination Act?
GIVEN
    `they acted as its employee or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person do it as the employer's employee or agent? (For a volunteer or unpaid trainee who sexually harassed you, the employer is the body they volunteer for.)
    `it would be unlawful if the employer did it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the act contravene the Act if the employer or principal had done it?
    `the employer authorised it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employer or principal authorise the act, expressly or by implication, before or after it was done? A judgment.
    `the employer took all reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employer or principal take all reasonable steps to prevent the employee or agent from contravening the Act? A judgment; the employer must prove it.
GIVETH A `Employer liability answer`
`Is my employer liable for what its employee did` `they acted as its employee or agent` `it would be unlawful if the employer did it` `the employer authorised it` `the employer took all reasonable steps` MEANS
    `the answer on the employer's liability` `they acted as its employee or agent` `it would be unlawful if the employer did it` `the employer authorised it` `the employer took all reasonable steps`

§ `Making a complaint`

@export Can this complaint be made to the President of the Anti-Discrimination Board, by me or by someone for me?
GIVEN
    `who complains`             IS A `Who makes the complaint` @desc Who is making the complaint?
    `it is an offence provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision said to be broken one for which the Act imposes a specific penalty (an offence, such as publishing a discriminatory advertisement)?
    `everyone consents`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a representative body: does each person on whose behalf it complains consent?
    `the body has a sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a representative body: is the President satisfied the conduct is a matter of genuine concern to the body because of how it affects the body or the group it represents? A judgment.
GIVETH A `Standing answer`
`Can this complaint be made` `who complains` `it is an offence provision` `everyone consents` `the body has a sufficient interest` MEANS
    `the answer on who may complain` `who complains` `it is an offence provision` `everyone consents` `the body has a sufficient interest`

@export By when must I lodge my complaint so that the President cannot decline it for being about conduct more than 12 months old?
GIVEN
    `the day it started`        IS A DATE @desc On what day did the earliest conduct you complain about happen?
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I lodge my complaint` `the day it started` MEANS
    `the last day to lodge for conduct on` `the day it started`

@export Is my complaint, made on this day, in time, or may the President decline it because the conduct is more than 12 months old?
GIVEN
    `the day it started`        IS A DATE @desc On what day did the earliest conduct you complain about happen?
    `the day it last happened`  IS A DATE @desc On what day did the latest conduct you complain about happen?
    `the day I lodge`           IS A DATE @desc On what day did you lodge (or will you lodge) the complaint with the President?
GIVETH A `Complaint time answer`
`Is my complaint in time` `the day it started` `the day it last happened` `the day I lodge` MEANS
    `the answer on lodging in time` `the day it started` `the day it last happened` `the day I lodge`

§ `After the President declines my complaint`
-- Situation: only if the President has given you a notice declining your complaint (s 87B(4) or s 92).

@export By when must I require the President to refer my declined complaint to the Civil and Administrative Tribunal?
GIVEN
    `it came by post`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice declining your complaint given by post?
    `the day of the notice`     IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice given (or, if it came by post, posted)?
    `weekday holidays`          IS A NUMBER @desc Only if it came by post: how many public or bank holidays (where the notice was sent) fell on weekdays in the working days after posting? Usually 0.
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I require referral to the Tribunal` `it came by post` `the day of the notice` `weekday holidays` MEANS
    `the last day to require referral` `it came by post` `the day of the notice` `weekday holidays`

@export Did I require the President to refer my declined complaint to the Tribunal in time?
GIVEN
    `it came by post`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice declining your complaint given by post?
    `the day of the notice`     IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice given (or, if it came by post, posted)?
    `weekday holidays`          IS A NUMBER @desc Only if it came by post: how many public or bank holidays (where the notice was sent) fell on weekdays in the working days after posting? Usually 0.
    `the day I required it`     IS A DATE @desc On what day did you give the President written notice requiring referral?
GIVETH A `Referral answer`
`Did I require referral in time` `it came by post` `the day of the notice` `weekday holidays` `the day I required it` MEANS
    `the answer on requiring referral` `it came by post` `the day of the notice` `weekday holidays` `the day I required it`

§ `When my complaint is still unresolved after 18 months`
-- Situation: only if your complaint has not been declined, terminated or resolved.

@export From what day can I ask for my unresolved complaint to be referred to the Tribunal?
GIVEN
    `the day I made it`         IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make (lodge) the complaint?
GIVETH A DATE
`From when can I ask for my unresolved complaint to be referred` `the day I made it` MEANS
    `the first day to request referral of an unresolved complaint made on` `the day I made it`

@export What happens when my complaint, unresolved after 18 months, is asked to be referred to the Tribunal?
GIVEN
    `it was resolved in time`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your complaint declined, terminated or otherwise resolved within 18 months after you made it?
    `the day I made it`         IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make the complaint?
    `the day of the request`    IS A DATE @desc On what day was referral requested?
    `who asked`                 IS A `Who asked for referral` @desc Who asked the President to refer it?
    `I objected`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you object to the referral within 28 days after the President's notice of the request?
    `the respondent objected`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the respondent object within those 28 days?
    `the President sees a reasonable prospect of agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the President satisfied there are reasonable prospects of a conciliated agreement? A judgment.
GIVETH A `Unresolved referral answer`
`What happens to my request for referral` `it was resolved in time` `the day I made it` `the day of the request` `who asked` `I objected` `the respondent objected` `the President sees a reasonable prospect of agreement` MEANS
    `the answer on referral of an unresolved complaint` `it was resolved in time` `the day I made it` `the day of the request` `who asked` `I objected` `the respondent objected` `the President sees a reasonable prospect of agreement`

§ `After a conciliation agreement`
-- Situation: only if your complaint was settled by agreement at conciliation.

@export By when must I apply to the Tribunal to register my conciliation agreement?
GIVEN
    `the day of the agreement`  IS A DATE @desc On what day was the agreement reached?
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply to register my agreement` `the day of the agreement` MEANS
    `the last day to apply to register an agreement made on` `the day of the agreement`

@export Can I apply to the Tribunal to register my conciliation agreement because the other side has not kept it?
GIVEN
    `it is recorded and signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement recorded in writing and signed by or for each party?
    `they have not complied`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you believe another party has not complied with its terms?
    `the day of the agreement`  IS A DATE @desc On what day was the agreement reached?
    `the day I apply`           IS A DATE @desc On what day do (or did) you apply?
GIVETH A `Registration answer`
`Can I register my agreement` `it is recorded and signed` `they have not complied` `the day of the agreement` `the day I apply` MEANS
    `the answer on registering the agreement` `it is recorded and signed` `they have not complied` `the day of the agreement` `the day I apply`

§ `After my complaint is taken to be abandoned`
-- Situation: only if the President served a notice that your complaint would be taken to be abandoned.

@export By when can I revive my complaint after it was taken to be abandoned?
GIVEN
    `the day of the notice`     IS A DATE @desc On what day was the President's 28-day abandonment notice served on you?
GIVETH A DATE
`By when can I revive my complaint` `the day of the notice` MEANS
    `the last day to revive a complaint whose abandonment notice was served on` `the day of the notice`

@export Can my complaint, taken to be abandoned, be revived?
GIVEN
    `the day of the notice`     IS A DATE @desc On what day was the President's 28-day abandonment notice served on you?
    `the day I satisfy the President` IS A DATE @desc On what day do (or did) you satisfy the President?
    `the President is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the President satisfied that you wish to pursue it, that the failure did not happen or ought reasonably to be excused, and that reviving it would cause the respondent no undue prejudice? A judgment.
GIVETH A `Revival answer`
`Can my complaint be revived` `the day of the notice` `the day I satisfy the President` `the President is satisfied` MEANS
    `the answer on reviving the complaint` `the day of the notice` `the day I satisfy the President` `the President is satisfied`

§ `What the Tribunal may award me`
-- Situation: only if the Tribunal finds your complaint substantiated.

@export What is the most the Tribunal can order the respondent to pay me in damages for my loss, in Australian dollars?
GIVEN
    `the Minister referred it`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the matter referred to the Tribunal by the Minister (rather than by the President on your complaint)?
    `my loss`                   IS A NUMBER  @desc How much loss or damage, in Australian dollars, does the Tribunal find you suffered because of the respondent's conduct?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The most I can be awarded for my loss` `the Minister referred it` `my loss` MEANS
    `the most the Tribunal may order for my loss` `the Minister referred it` `my loss`

@export If the respondent fails to comply with a non-money order of the Tribunal, what is the most it can be made to pay me for that, in Australian dollars?
GIVEN
    `there is an unmet default order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Tribunal, with an order to stop, redress, apologise or adopt a program, also order damages in default of compliance, and has the respondent failed to comply?
    `my loss from the failure`  IS A NUMBER  @desc How much loss, in Australian dollars, does the Tribunal find the failure to comply caused you?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The most I can be awarded for a failure to comply` `there is an unmet default order` `my loss from the failure` MEANS
    `the most for failure to comply` `there is an unmet default order` `my loss from the failure`

@export Will the damages the Tribunal orders be paid to me?
GIVEN
    `a representative body complained for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the complaint made by a representative body on your behalf?
    `I was an offender in custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the conduct that of a protected defendant (such as the State or a corrections body) while you were an offender in custody?
GIVETH A `Who receives the damages`
`Will the damages be paid to me` `a representative body complained for me` `I was an offender in custody` MEANS
    `the answer on who receives the damages` `a representative body complained for me` `I was an offender in custody`
